%I A401751 #10 Nov 05 2026 05:52:42
%S A401751 4,12,20,28,44,52,60,68,76,84,92,116,124,132,140,148,156,164,172,188,
%T A401751 200,204,212,220,228,236,244,260,268,276,284,292,308,316,332,340,348,
%U A401751 356,364,372,380,388,404,412,420,428,436,444,452,460,476,492,508,516,524
%N A401751 Numbers k such that A051377(k) = 3*k/2.
%C A401751 First differs from its subsequence A081770 at n = 21: a(21) = 200 is not a term in A081770.
%C A401751 The relative asymptotic density of A081770 within this sequence is 1/(Pi^2*d) = 0.981738..., where d is the asymptotic density of this sequence that is mentioned below.
%C A401751 First differs from A401189 at n = 21: a(21) = 200 is not a term in A401189. Differs from A401189 by having the terms 200, 600, 1400, 1936, 2200, ..., and not having the terms 648, 3240, 4536, 5184, 7128, ... .
%C A401751 Differs from A364999 by having the terms 4, 200, 600, 1004, 1012, 1020, 1028, 1036, 1052, 1060, ... .
%C A401751 Equivalently, numbers k such that A126164(k) = k/2.
%C A401751 All the terms are even by definition.
%C A401751 All the terms are nonsquarefree (A013929), since A051377(k) = k for squarefree numbers k.
%C A401751 Analogous to e-perfect numbers (A054979), which have a ratio A051377(k)/k = 2 instead of 3/2.
%C A401751 Analogous to hemiperfect numbers (A159907) with the sum of exponential divisors (A051377) instead of the sum of divisors (A000203). Are there numbers k with half-integer values of A051377(k)/k other than 3/2? There are none below 10^20.
%C A401751 If m is a term, and k is a squarefree number coprime to m, then k*m is also a term.
%C A401751 The primitive terms in this sequence are the powerful terms (A401752). This sequence can be generated from the primitive terms by multiplying with coprime squarefree numbers.
%C A401751 The asymptotic density of this sequence is Sum_{n>=1} f(A401752(n)) = 0.103205885391556235..., where  f(n) = (6/(Pi^2*n)) * Product_{prime p|n} (p/(p+1)).
%H A401751 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A401751/b401751.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%t A401751 f[p_, e_] := DivisorSum[e, p^# &]; esigma[1] = 1; esigma[n_] := Times @@ f @@@ FactorInteger[n]; q[k_] := esigma[k] == 3*k/2; Select[2 * Range[265], q]
%o A401751 (PARI) isok(k) = if(k%2, 0, vecprod([sumdiv(f[2], d, f[1]^d) | f <- factor(k)~]) == 3*k/2);
%Y A401751 Subsequence of A005843 and A013929.
%Y A401751 Subsequences: A081770, A401752.
%Y A401751 Cf. A000203, A005117, A051377, A054979, A126164, A159907.
%Y A401751 Cf. A364999, A401189.
%K A401751 nonn,easy,new
%O A401751 1,1
